{
  "category": "Iron Armor Pokémon",
  "entries": [
    {
      "text": "This POKéMON has a body of steel. To make its body, ARON feeds on iron ore that it digs from mountains. Occasionally, it causes major trouble by eating bridges and rails.",
      "version": "ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "ARON has a body of steel. With one all-out charge, this POKéMON can demolish even a heavy dump truck. The destroyed dump truck then becomes a handy meal for the POKéMON.",
      "version": "sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "A POKéMON that is clad in steel armor. A new suit of armor is made when it evolves. The old, discarded armor is salvaged as metal for making iron products.",
      "version": "emerald"
    },
    {
      "text": "It eats iron to build its steel body. It is a pest that descends from mountains to eat bridges and train tracks.",
      "version": "firered"
    },
    {
      "text": "It eats iron to build its steel body. It is a pest that descends from mountains to eat bridges and train tracks.",
      "version": "leafgreen"
    },
    {
      "text": "It usually lives deep in mountains. However, hunger may drive it to eat railroad tracks and cars.",
      "version": "diamond"
    },
    {
      "text": "It usually lives deep in mountains. However, hunger may drive it to eat railroad tracks and cars.",
      "version": "pearl"
    },
    {
      "text": "It usually lives deep in mountains. However, hunger may drive it to eat railroad tracks and cars.",
      "version": "platinum"
    },
    {
      "text": "When it evolves, it sheds the steel carapace that covered its whole body and develops a new one.",
      "version": "heartgold"
    },
    {
      "text": "When it evolves, it sheds the steel carapace that covered its whole body and develops a new one.",
      "version": "soulsilver"
    },
    {
      "text": "It usually lives deep in mountains. However, hunger may drive it to eat railroad tracks and cars.",
      "version": "black"
    },
    {
      "text": "It usually lives deep in mountains. However, hunger may drive it to eat railroad tracks and cars.",
      "version": "white"
    },
    {
      "text": "In order to build up its steel body, it eats iron ore. This pesky Pokémon is known to eat railroad tracks.",
      "version": "black-2"
    },
    {
      "text": "In order to build up its steel body, it eats iron ore. This pesky Pokémon is known to eat railroad tracks.",
      "version": "white-2"
    },
    {
      "text": "It usually lives deep in mountains. However, hunger may drive it to eat railroad tracks and cars.",
      "version": "x"
    },
    {
      "text": "When it evolves, it sheds the steel carapace that covered its whole body and develops a new one.",
      "version": "y"
    },
    {
      "text": "This Pokémon has a body of steel. To make its body, Aron feeds on iron ore that it digs from mountains. Occasionally, it causes major trouble by eating bridges and rails.",
      "version": "omega-ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "Aron has a body of steel. With one all-out charge, this Pokémon can demolish even a heavy dump truck. The destroyed dump truck then becomes a handy meal for the Pokémon.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "It eats iron ore—and sometimes railroad tracks— to build up the steel armor that protects its body.",
      "version": "sword"
    },
    {
      "text": "When Aron evolves, its steel armor peels off. In ancient times, people would collect Aron’s shed armor and make good use of it in their daily lives.",
      "version": "shield"
    }
  ],
